title: nemesis2_price
---
Narrator:
The download completes.

---

Narrator:
Your security officer does not speak immediately. She reads for a long time.

When she speaks, her voice is level. That is the most troubling thing about it.

---

Narrator:
She says: the archive contains everything.

She says: the campaigns, the outcomes, the patterns. It contains projections — models of where this conflict ends if current trajectories hold.

---

Narrator:
She says: none of the projections end well.

She does not say for whom.

---

Narrator:
The archive also contains a second set of files. Sealed. They are addressed to you, specifically.

To your name.

Not your rank. Your name.

---

-> [Open the sealed files]
    <<apply_effect "blood_price">>
    Narrator:
    You open them alone.

    Narrator:
    You do not share what is inside.

    Narrator:
    When your security officer asks what they contained, you tell her: strategic assessments. Nothing actionable.

    Narrator:
    She knows you're lying. She lets it go.

    Narrator:
    You proceed to the next system carrying something you cannot put down.

-> [Destroy the sealed files — don't look]
    <<apply_effect "inner_sanctum_key">>
    Narrator:
    You delete them without reading.

    Narrator:
    Your security officer says nothing. She files the action under "command discretion."

    Narrator:
    For three days you wonder what was in them.

    Narrator:
    On the fourth day, you stop wondering.

    Narrator:
    That is either discipline or loss.

    Narrator:
    You're no longer sure of the difference.

===
